**Read:** [Planning and interpreting XPS — Baer and colleagues](../sources/XPS-Planning-Interpretation-and-Reporting-Baer.lingua#r_6CY69TZ791W5PW0SZCY536SVH5) and [Attenuation and information depth in XPS — Cedric Powell](../sources/XPS-Attenuation-and-Information-Depth-Powell.lingua#r_0RF0DVE5MXB1BAG8S0W48X46TV); [Nonvolatile residue collection and analysis — Gordon, Rutherford and Aranda](../sources/Nonvolatile-Residue-Collection-and-Analysis-NASA.lingua#r_2YMCRSWR07NCHECM0X4D8FJ6HJ), main account of collection, gravimetry and chemical evidence. Read [Analytical Chemistry 2.1 — David Harvey](../../../chemistry/general-chemistry/sources/Analytical-Chemistry-Harvey.lingua#r_0XMY75E3FRXRGR3BK28V3JAC0T), chapters 5, 7, 10 and 12 progressively with the analytical material below.

The aerosol section observed material carried in gas. The next question is what remains on an object, where it is, and whether it changes the object's useful function. A visible particle, an extracted residue and a surface-sensitive spectrum observe different parts of that question.

Begin with sampling and specimen history, then images, recovery, spectra, separation and calibration. Surface-sensitive electrons lead into depth weighting, film thickness and heterogeneous surfaces. Three investigations combine spatial observation, residue analysis and film inference.

Use benign mathematical examples and published observations for the studies. Practical measurements involving hazardous specimens, solvents, radiation or energized instruments require the relevant competence and facility controls. Their operational procedures are not needed to follow the measurement arguments here.

**Work:** Choose an ordinary object and a defined useful function. Draw where an unwanted material could be located and propose complementary observations. Identify which claims concern the surface itself, which concern a collected sample, and which require a separate functional test.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
**Continue in clean manufacturing:** [A measurement observes a filtered field](../../../engineering/materials-engineering/research/A-measurement-observes-a-filtered-field.lingua#r_4P5XG26ENMZPFN5ED5HXZRWCV7).

